WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.960
Jev needs Jeeves.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.080
So does your to-do list.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.500
Here's how they work together.

00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:09.588
Start with a request.

00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:13.648
Each agent gets a clear job, and you can see every step.

00:00:14.428 --> 00:00:16.388
This run uses Jev and Codex.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:21.324
Jev spots an outage and chooses the urgent route.

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:26.004
Open the decision to see its answer, confidence, and the path it picked.

00:00:27.684 --> 00:00:30.344
Now try a request that's missing the details.

00:00:31.304 --> 00:00:34.424
Jeeves asks a question, saves the run, and waits.

00:00:35.284 --> 00:00:37.244
No answer, no next step.

00:00:38.908 --> 00:00:40.948
Add what's missing and hit submit.

00:00:41.728 --> 00:00:43.688
The next agent can now get to work.

00:00:45.356 --> 00:00:50.676
Here's the result: a concrete action brief, a suggested fix, and a draft reply.

00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:52.936
It's ready for your review.

00:00:53.756 --> 00:00:54.876
Nothing has been sent.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.860
Save the workflow for next time, or export it as a portable skill.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.340
Next Tuesday is already looking a little more organised.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.760
Jev makes the judgment.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.440
Jeeves keeps things moving.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.060
Open source, on your desktop.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.400
Very good, then.

